### Reference discipline

- Encyclopedia `sources`, `sourceFile`, selectors, manifests, certificates, and generated indexes must name the exact publication path above.
- Lean and Rust files may cite these papers as provenance, but a path update cannot change theorem status. `omega_engine/research/published/GTOC_LEAN4_SOURCE_MAP.md` binds each publication to its current Lean obligation ids. A future `lean_ref` must name an actual built theorem and preserve every paper hypothesis.
- The companion ledger is not a second authority surface. Any paper/ledger mismatch is an obstruction and blocks publication status until reconciled.
- Retired control artifacts and the former `_archive/` inputs remain deleted; their live rules are in this charter and `theorem_ledger.md`.

New proof obligations opened by the series are recorded in `omega_engine/research/encyclopedia/proof_ledgers/proof_ledger_20260713.md` (PL-GTOC-1..13; the earlier `PL-GTOCF-*` prefix is retired), `proof_ledger_20260715.md` (PL-GTOC-14..20 plus amendments), and `proof_ledger_20260717.md` (the PL-GTOC-9 representation amendment and PL-GTOC-28..33). The merged Phase 3 spine reserves PL-GTOC-21..27; their missing authoritative long statements remain an explicit ledger-reconciliation defect.
